To calculate the mass of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose of Pa-Fi.

First, we need to convert the percentage from a percentage of weight per volume to a fraction of weight per volume:  
0.044% (v/v) = 0.044 grams of sodium fluoride per 100 grams of Pa-Fl.

Now, we can calculate the mass of sodium fertilizer in a 10 mL dose:  
\[
\text{Mass of sodium fluoride} = \frac{0.044 \text{ g}}{100 \text{ g}} \times 10 \text{ mL}
\]  
\[
\text{Mass of sodium fluoride} = 0.0044 \text{ g}
\]  
Finally, we need to convert the mass from grams to milligrams:  
\[
\text{Mass of sodium fluoride in milligrams} = 0.0044 \text{ g} \times 1000 \text{ mg per g} = 4.4 \text{ mg}
\]  
Thus, there are $\boxed{4.4}$ milligrams of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose of Pa-Fl.
