The relationship between \([H_3O^+]\) and \([H_2O^+]\) is given by:
\[
\frac{[H_3O^+]}{[\text{H}_2O^+]} = 10^{-14}
\]
The density of hydrogen oxide is approximately 10^-12 M. Therefore, the definition of atomic-specific-density of hydrogen oxygen is:
\[
\text{ADS} = \frac{[H_3O^+]}{10^{-12}}
\]
Substituting the given value of \([H_3O^+]\) into the equation:
\[
\text{ADS} = \frac{10^{-4}}{10^{-12}} = 10^{-4 + 12} = 10^8
\]
