\[
\text{M} = \frac{\text{N}}{\text{H}_2O_4}
\]

Since H\(_2</sub>O\(_4\\) is a diatomic solution, the molar mass is 2.

1. **Calculate the total mass of H\(_2\\)SO\(_4\\) in the 10.0 L of 2.00 N H\(_2\\)SO\(_4\):**
   \[
