\[
\text{Δ = } \text{Ox} - \text{Ca} = 1.65 - 1.55 = 0.1
\]

A small difference in electronegizability (0.1) indicates that the bond is **slightly polar**. Oxygen is more electronegisable than calcium, so the oxygen atoms will have a negative polarity, and the carbon atom will have a positive polarity.

\[
\text{CO = 0.1}
\]

