$$(a_{1}+2a_{2}+4a_{3}+…+2^{n-1}a_{n})=2n-1.$$
For $n=1$, we have $a_{1}=2-1=1$.
For $n=2$, we have $a_{1}+2a_{2}=2\times2-1=3$, which gives $1+2a_{2}=3$, so $a_{2}=1$.
For $n=3$, we have $a_{1}+2a_{2}+4a_{3}=2\times3-1=5$, which gives $1+2+4a_{3}=5$, so $a_{3}=1$.
