   Since \( A \triangle B \subseteq A \), every element \( x \) in \( A \triangle B \) must also be in \( A \).

4. **Analyze \( A \triangle B \):**
   - If \( x \in A \triangle B \), then \( x \in (A \setminus B) \cup (B \setminus A) \).
   - This implies either \( x \in A \setminus B \) or \( x \in B \setminus A \).

