The index of resistance \( F \) is defined as the ratio of the speed of light in a fluid to the speed of light in a medium of least resistance (i.e., water).

\[
F = \frac{\text{Speed of light in fluid}}{\text{Speed of light in medium of least resistance}}
\]

For the given problem, the medium of least resistance is a vacuum, and the speed of light in a vacuum is \( 1.6 \times 10^9 \times \mathrm{m/s} \). The speed of light in the pipe is \( 0.680 \times 1.6 \times 10^9 \times \mathrm{m/s} \).

Thus, the index of resistance is:

\[
F = \frac{0.680 \times 1.6 \times 10^9 \times \mathrm{m/s}}{1.6 \times 10^9 \times \mathrm{m/s}} = 0.680
\]

Thus, the index of resistance for yellow light in the pipe is \( 0.680 \).
