","(a) The force done by the electric field is given by:  
\[ F = N \times I = 1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C} \times 500 \, \text{N/C} = 800 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{N} = 800 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{N} \]  
The acceleration of the projectile is then:  
\[ a = \frac{F}{v} = \frac{800 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{N}}{1.67 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{kg}} = 4.81 \times 10^{8} \, \text{m/s}^2 \]  
(b) The particle is accelerated from rest, so \( v_0 = 0 \). Using the equation \( v = v_0 + at \), we solve for \( t \):  
\[ t = \frac{v - v_0}{a} = \frac{35,000 \, \text{m/s} - 0 \, \text{m/s}}{4.81 \times 10^8 \, \text{m/s}^2} = \frac{35,000 \, \text{m/s}}{4.81 \times 10^8 \, \text{m/s}^2} = 72 \times 10^{-6} \, \text{s} = 72 \, \text{s} \]  
(a) The magnitude of the acceleration of the projectile is \( \boxed{4.81 \times 10^8 \, \text{m/s}^2} \).  
